 specimens were annealed and dried at 80 °C for 12 h before testing","source":"B-paht-cf-TDS","at":"Test specimen preparation","domain":"Post-processing","type":"Manufacturer statement","category":"specimen-prep","conditions":"TDS specimen conditioning. Do not confuse with a general annealing schedule."}]},{"topic":"Post-processing","items":[{"id":"Q00532","text":"the suggested annealing temperature of models printed with Bambu PAHT-CF is 80 to 130 °C, and the time is 6 to 12 hours.","source":"B-paht-cf-TDS","at":"p. 3: Annealing note","domain":"Post-processing","type":"Manufacturer statement","category":"post-processing","conditions":"Annealing the printed part: 80 to 130 °C, 6 to 12 hours"}]},{"topic":"Good for","items":[{"id":"Q03405","text":"Suggested uses are: functional prototypes, machining fixtures, injection molds, jigs, and low-volume production parts.","source":"B-paht-cf-TDS","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q03406","text":"Bambu PAHT-CF is a high-temperature engineering-grade carbon-fiber reinforced nylon that is designed for applications where high strength, stiffness, and temperature resistance are required.","source":"B-paht-cf-TDS","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Pitfalls and limitations","items":[{"id":"Q05685","text":"As this filament contains highly hygroscopic wood fibers, please place any unused filament in a sealed container with desiccant immediately, and dry thoroughly before printing.","source":"R-BAMBU-PRIORITY-20261003-a100c1bb3a92","at":"p. 1: exact product features/description/application tips, source text line 176","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement","conditions":"Copied wood-fibre sentence on PAHT-CF page; not evidence of wood filler/composition. Own humidity guidance remains separate; maker clarification needed."}]},{"topic":"Adhesion between layers","items":[{"id":"Q03407","text":"It is easy to print, has enhanced Z-bonding, a high-degree of dimensional stability, and has been optimized to retain excellent mechanical properties when wet.","source":"B-paht-cf-TDS","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Odour and emissions","items":[{"id":"Q03409","text":"Odor Odorless","source":"B-paht-cf-TDS","at":"p. 3","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Supports and removal","items":[{"id":"Q03408","text":"Support Material Bambu Support for PA/PET","source":"B-paht-cf-TDS","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05684","text":"When printing a model with support, we recommend removing the support structures within 2 hours after printing to prevent them from sticking after absorbing moisture. If sticking occurs, dry the model to ease the removal.","source":"R-BAMBU-PRIORITY-20261003-a100c1bb3a92","at":"p. 1: exact product features/description/application tips, source text line 166","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement","conditions":"Own2hour removal recommendation avoids moisture sticking; no universal post-processing or hydrolysis property."}]}]},{"id":"G048-02","name":"BASF Forward AM Ultrafuse PAHT CF15","maker":"BASF Forward AM","variant":null,"diameter":"1.75 mm","twins":[],"composition":"High-temperature polyamide filled with 15 % carbon fibres (TDS p. 1, Components)","certifications":"ESD-safe claimed at a surface resistivity of 1e5 to 1e11 ohm (TDS p. 1); no printed-part certification stated","availability":"Current official product listing retrieved 2026-09-17","claim":null,"values":[{"key":"density","id":"V012681","value":1203,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-BASF-ExtendedTDS-Ultrafuse-PAHT-CF15-V1-5","page":4,"twin":null,"at":"Filament Density"},{"key":"tensileModulusXY","id":"V002469","value":8.386,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-FORWARDAM-PAHT-CF15-TDS-v4